@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+No: the proposed direct-score replacement does not preserve the sealed three-route experiment unchanged; a different deployment can preserve three source interventions, conditionally.
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM` — design analysis, 2026-09-10. The reported direct-prediction ranking advantage is accepted as given. No training, policy evaluation, or acceptance test was run. This note is the only file written; sealed material is unchanged.
+
+**Q1. Where the three routes enter today.** Verified in code: the relevant implementation is `V1ThreeRouteModel` and `ProfileSelector`, not the older compatibility `ThreeRouteModel`/`DeploymentAdapter`. The model contains `q1`, `q2`, and `psi`; C1/C2 accept action-state vectors, while C3 requires a complete coalition context. The compatibility per-action C3 batch is explicitly excluded from contract-v1 training. [learner.py:175](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:175), [learner.py:930](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:930).
+
+For a candidate profile `a` and reference `a0`, define the deployed predictions
+
+```
+u_i(a) = q1(table_i.q1_states[a_i]) - q1(table_i.q1_states[a0_i])
+v_i(a) = q2(table_i.q2_states[a_i]) - q2(table_i.q2_states[a0_i])
+p(a)   = psi(coalition_context[a])
+S3(a)  = sum_i u_i(a) + sum_i v_i(a) + p(a).
+```
+
+`_additive_score` consumes the two action-state tables; `select` adds `model.interaction(context)`, filters legality/service, and chooses the first strict maximum with BASE first. These are predictions of the declared targets; the exact target identity does not make the learned predictions exact. [deployment.py:626](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:626), [deployment.py:710](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:710).
+
+| Route | Training tensor and target | Path to the committed configuration |
+|---|---|---|
+| C1 | `PairwiseBatch.reference_states`, `candidate_states`, `target_deltas` train `q1`. The target is immediate whole-network bit/energy surplus divided by κ, plus the existing signed Φ difference. | Each `u_i` enters every candidate's score. The same `q1` action outputs also enter per-user `argmax(Q1+Q2)` and the sum used to repair an infeasible proposal. Neutral training can therefore alter ranking and, when that proposal builder is actually called, the reference and fallback profile. |
+| C2 | The corresponding pairwise tensors train `q2` on the three-offset continuation surplus with absorbing lost-offset penalties, excluding the immediate term. | Each `v_i` enters candidate ranking and the same proposal/repair computations. Neutral training can change those decisions independently of C1. |
+| C3 | `CoalitionBatch.invariant_states` and `target_psi` train `psi.network` on the normalized interaction residual. | `psi.score(context)` supplies one complete-set scalar to ranking. It is hard zero for empty/singleton sets. C3 does not enter the Q1+Q2 proposal/repair helper. Neutral training can change which joint profile wins. |
+
+Target definitions: [targets.py:154](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:154), [targets.py:251](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:251), [targets.py:602](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:602). Tensor construction and losses: [learner.py:70](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:70), [learner.py:543](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:543), [learner.py:778](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:778), [learner.py:827](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:827). Proposal and repair: [deployment.py:511](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:511).
+
+The actual neutral substitution preserves action/context inputs and row identities while replacing `target_deltas` or `target_psi` with zeros. It changes training, not deployment by hard-zeroing an output. All five learned arms clone one initialization and update all three heads; `SOURCE_MAP` changes only the named route's source in each DROP. At a fixed supplied context, the other independently trained heads therefore have the same parameters as FULL. A neutral-trained prediction need not be exactly zero, and a changed prediction need not change the winning profile. [learner.py:26](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:26), [learner.py:146](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:146), [learner.py:634](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:634), [learner.py:994](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:994).
+
+Two implementation details determine whether indirect paths exist:
+
+- `select` receives `base_profile`; it does not invoke `repair_reference`. It authenticates the supplied reference against coordinator information and every coalition context. Merely retaining the helper does not establish that any arm uses its own learned proposal. The pilot builds contexts before the arm loop from a shared anchor. [deployment.py:589](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:589), [deployment.py:647](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:647), [run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1503](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1503).
+- `CoalitionMember.selected_q1_row` and `incumbent_q1_row` are raw Q1 state vectors, not Q1 predictions. The invariant tensor pools these vectors, physical-action information, affected-resource features, cross-gain terms and global context. It contains neither learned Q1 outputs nor learned Q2 outputs. Keeping this tensor does not keep either learned source route. [coalitions.py:36](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/coalitions.py:36), [coalitions.py:240](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/coalitions.py:240), [run_v025_pilot_c3.py:844](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:844).
+
+**Q2. Where routes could enter a direct score.** Let `J(a;a0)` denote the stored normalized joint objective change, with existing Φ accounting retained. It replaces the immediate C1-plus-interaction target, not C2's continuation target. The code stores both Φ-inclusive and physical identities separately. [coalitions.py:311](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/coalitions.py:311), [targets.py:599](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:599). The following decision-path consequences are design inferences from the verified implementation.
+
+1. **Raw-context direct head, fixed shared reference: `S=D(Z,a0,A,a_A)`.** C1 and C2 disappear from ranking and proposal generation. Their neutral substitutions change unused head parameters but cannot change committed configurations through the policy. Calling raw Q1/Q2 fields “route features” does not restore source effects. C3 can affect ranking if its source now trains `D`, but it has become joint-objective supervision. This is the relevant trap in the measured DIRECT implementation: its Q1 feature bank uses feature moments and fixed random weights, and DIRECT predicts from that feature matrix without consuming the separately fitted additive head. [compare_target_parametrisations.py:441](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py:441), [compare_target_parametrisations.py:1010](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py:1010), [compare_target_parametrisations.py:1030](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py:1030).
+
+2. **Replace only the immediate pair: `S=D+sum_i v_i`.** C2 retains its original continuation source and direct ranking path. C1 is still disconnected at a fixed reference unless another path is added. C3's training target is still changed from Ψ to J. Adding `sum_i u_i` as well would restore C1 mechanically, but count unilateral immediate value again; that is not the stated replacement.
+
+3. **C1/C2 survive only through arm-specific proposal and repair.** Each arm must actually compute `a0_r=repair(argmax(q1_r+q2_r))` with its own retained heads. Neutral training can then alter BASE, the changed-user set/context, BASE tie preference, reference-relative guard inputs and timeout fallback. Those are real paths to a different commit. Identical authenticated catalogues must still be maintained at matched anchors; silently changing candidate coverage would introduce another intervention. If `sum_i v_i` remains in the score, C2 additionally retains its ranking path. If it is removed, C2 has only the proposal path and its continuation value no longer directly scores candidates. The underlying reference, matching and fallback requirements are [contract §A3–A4:8](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:8), [contract §F2:39](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:39).
+
+   A different reference does **not** guarantee a different winner: with exact `J=F(a)/κ−F(a0)/κ`, a fixed candidate set and fixed feasible set, changing `a0` only subtracts a candidate-independent constant. Only approximation/context dependence, changed admissibility, ties or fallback can then transmit the reference change. A shared external/FULL proposal erases the DROP head's proposal path altogether.
+
+4. **Learned route outputs become direct-head inputs.** A new `D` could consume pooled, paired predictions `q1_r(selected/reference)` and `q2_r(selected/reference)` alongside the physical set context. Neutral C1/C2 training would change those activations and could change ranking, even with a fixed reference. They must be the current arm's outputs; precomputing FULL's predictions for all arms removes this intervention. If preserving route-local training, direct-loss gradients must not retrain Q1/Q2 through a different supervision path. C3 can train `D` on J, but that still changes C3's specified source. This input wiring is absent from the current invariant tensor and fixed `CoalitionBatch.invariant_states`.
+
+5. **Original Ψ survives as an input to a separate direct readout.** Retain Q1, Q2 and Ψ with their original informative/neutral training, then consume their outputs in a common direct readout. All three source substitutions can have live paths. This differs from replacing Ψ's training target; Q4 describes the construction and its cost.
+
+6. **An apparent decomposition obtained by cancellation.** Writing `psi_effective=D−sum_i u_i` and retaining the old sum yields `S=D+sum_i v_i`. It does not preserve C1's ranking effect unless `D` independently consumes C1 predictions. C1 survives only through any genuinely executed proposal path. Subtracting C2 inside the same compensation cancels C2 too. A head name or a reported decomposition is not a causal path.
+
+**Q3. Does the ablation mean the same thing?** The sealed sentence concerns informative versus specified neutral **source training**, with other routes informative and all heads retained. It does not require each route to be an additive score term. Oracle factor removal and checkpoint knockout are expressly separate experiments. [contract §C3:21](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:21). Consequently:
+
+| Possibility | Status of the source-benefit sentence |
+|---|---|
+| Disconnected C1/C2 in option 1; disconnected C1 in option 2; cancelled routes in option 6 | **False as a positive causal claim** when no other path exists: the intervention cannot affect the policy. The arm contrast remains numerically measurable, but its policy-mediated effect is structurally zero under matched execution. |
+| C2 retained additively in option 2 | **Same source-claim meaning remains testable** for C2, conditional on the new deployment. Positivity is unestablished. |
+| Original C1/C2 used only for proposal/repair in option 3 | **Same literal source-claim meaning remains testable**, if the paths operate. A positive result would concern source-trained proposal/repair/fallback quality. Describing it as an additive scoring contribution would be a different claim. |
+| Original C1/C2 predictions used by `D` in option 4 | **Same literal source-claim meaning remains testable** if their original source definitions and dose remain intact. The mechanism becomes learned features used by a joint predictor. |
+| Ψ-trained C3 replaced by J-trained `D` in options 1–4 | **Different specified-source claim.** It compares joint-objective supervision with its neutral alternative, rather than interaction-residual supervision with the sealed neutral source. Keeping the name C3 does not preserve its target identity. |
+| Original three sources plus common readout in option 5 | **Same three literal source contrasts remain testable**, conditional on an additional fixed learned component. This is a different deployed system and control background. |
+
+“Remains testable” is not “remains true”: no design analysis establishes improved pooled EE. Nor does a live route establish FULL > each DROP > ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL. The positive conjunction and ordering require their own paired pooled-efficiency results; direct ranking superiority alone settles none of them. §C5 fixes source generator, labels, support, strata, overlap, weights and optimization dose, and requires neutral-head updates and deployment participation. Those identities cannot be inferred from retained head names. [contract §C5:23](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:23), [learner.py:487](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:487).
+
+**Q4. Can a formulation keep both?** There is a precise prospective construction that combines direct prediction with the original three source interventions. There is **no verified formulation that also retains the sealed deployment unchanged and inherits the measured ranking gain**.
+
+The construction is a shared direct readout `H_phi`, with the original route heads retained:
+
+```
+q1_r, q2_r, psi_r: original route-local targets and SOURCE_MAP training
+u_i^r, v_i^r, p^r: each arm's own predictions defined in Q1
+
+D_r(a) = H_phi(Z, a0, A, a_A, {u_i^r(a)}, p^r(a))
+S_r(a) = D_r(a) + sum_i v_i^r(a)
+```
+
+Train `H_phi` directly against J on declared development data, then hold its parameters and training provenance identical across all five learned arms within a lineage. Preserve Q1/Q2/Ψ training and their neutral sources; do not backpropagate the new loss into them. Readout training must cover the declared informative/neutral input conditions, and inference must use each arm's actual outputs, never a substituted informative copy. `D(empty)=0`; singleton direct values are allowed to be nonzero. Q2's continuation remains outside the immediate joint predictor, so no horizon or immediate/continuation accounting is changed. This is a proposed formulation, not existing code.
+
+C1 then enters `H_phi` through `u_i`, C3 through `p`, and C2 through `sum v_i`; proposal/repair can remain additional paths. A readout can still learn to ignore an input, or learn compensating dependencies, so actual decision sensitivity and positive source marginals remain empirical requirements. Retaining inputs alone proves neither.
+
+The cost is an additional learned component and joint-label training source, a new input/target/checkpoint interface, support for singleton direct predictions, and new deployment evidence. ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL would be neutral for the **three original routes** while still containing informative common readout training. Thus the same literal source-benefit sentence is conditional on that shared predictor; it cannot describe an unchanged three-head system with all learned supervision neutral. The current model inventory and route-local updates contain no such readout. [learner.py:930](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:930), [learner.py:1021](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:1021).
+
+A three-head alternative—train `D` on `exact_C1 + psi_source`, using Ψ for the informative source and zero for neutral—gives J versus exact-C1 targets. It preserves an interaction-information contrast algebraically, but supplies unilateral supervision even to neutral C3. That changes the sealed labels, neutral training and control background. It is not unchanged C3-versus-zero training. Similarly, retaining Ψ as an auxiliary reporting head while bypassing its output does not preserve its source effect.
+
+Under the fixed project requirements, neither construction is a conforming replacement. §B4 fixes the factor identity, §C1 fixes the Q1/Q2 surrogate, and §C2 fixes residual-only C3 supervision, singleton zero anchoring and the deployed sum. A direct J predictor generally has nonzero singleton and additive-case values, unlike Ψ. Keeping the exact decomposition as a reporting KAT would not make a different deployed score satisfy §C2. [contract §B4:15](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:15), [contract §C1–C2:19](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:19), [learner.py:835](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:835). The observed gain belongs to the measured DIRECT model; its transfer to either source-preserving construction is unverified.
+
+**Q5. What would break.** For the prospectively measurable variants above, these are hypothetical replacement-evidence requirements, not changes authorized or performed here. Existing sealed artefacts remain historical evidence; their write-once implementation rejects overwriting. [canonical.py:73](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/canonical.py:73).
