+| Artefact or authority | Consequence |
+|---|---|
+| Sealed score/head/source specification and its contract hash | None of the changed direct selectors is certified by the existing §B4/§C2 seal. C3 retargeting also conflicts with §C5's specified source. Regenerating a manifest cannot repair that incompatibility. |
+| C3 rows, context schemas, shards and target batches | Rebinding `objective_delta_normalized_hex` as the target requires a new target/batch identity; it cannot retain the Ψ-batch meaning. Existing rows already contain J and need not be recomputed merely to read that field. True singleton support requires a new row/encoder path: current C3 rows reject size <2, the invariant encoder zeroes singleton member features, and the head hard-zeros their output. New learned-output inputs require a distinct context/readout schema and digest. Current names are `mcrl-v025-stagec-c3-coalition-{context,row,shard}-v2` and `mcrl-v025-stagec-c3-coalition-batch-v2`. |
+| Source definitions, source-authority and batch digests | Retargeted C3 needs new informed-target authority and any changed neutral-source definition/support/dose digest. The shared-readout construction can retain the original three source bytes and digests, but needs its own readout source/support/target authority. Arm-dependent predictions cannot be disguised as identical precomputed batches. |
+| Initialization, trainer and checkpoint manifests | Changed head inventory/input dimensions/target bindings need new initialization, serialized parameters and optimizer state, batch bindings and checkpoint digests. A shared readout must be explicitly bound as identical across arms. Original standalone route checkpoints can remain authentic inputs; the composite deployed checkpoint is new. |
+| Code, deployment capability, experiment and execution manifests | New code/checkpoint identity and measured latency require new deployment-capability evidence; changed experiment definitions need new bindings/digests. Allocation/launch authority, matched-information authentication, conformance authority, attempts, step/unit receipts and merged reports must bind the actual new system. Pilot `PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-{rows,training,evaluation}-manifest.json` files cannot certify it. |
